        "paragraphs": [
          "In 1786 Scipione de’ Ricci, bishop of Pistoia and Prato, held a diocesan synod that became a symbol of late Jansenist, regalistic, and ‘reform’ Catholicism in Tuscany. The synod’s acts touched the constitution of the Church, the authority of the pope and bishops, the liturgy, popular devotions, and the sacraments. Supporters saw pastoral purification; Rome saw a program that undermined hierarchy and dogma under the language of reform."
        ]
